WhAt'S rEfEr ?
-*-*-*-*-*-*-*

 >Refer< is basically a door to refer users to the sysop on closed boards.
The user can give global informations about his friend, then the door
writes a messy to the sysop and the sysop can decide wether he will or
not open access for the user. The door can also send EALL messages, so the
users can tell the sysop wether the user is good or not.

 >Refer< is able to write a messy to any user specified in the config
icon and not only to the sysop. This allow the sysop to have the point
of vue of other users/co-sysops. That's the only use as only the sysop
can create an access. If you specify EALL as name, then the door will
create... EALL messages ;)   The contents are a bit different and this way
your users can tell you what they think about the refered user.


'bOuT tHe ToOlTyPeS & iNsTaLlAtIoN
*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-

 Make a directory REFER in your DOORS:  drawer (must be assigned) and copy
the door in it + its icon. Put in your BBS:Commands/BBSCmd drawer the door
icon like for all doors. And again... if you don't have the AEDoor.Library
by Sintax/WoT installed, don't expect the door to work !

 Sysops using /X v1.x -> 2.x will know better than me how to configurate
the whole thing. The only thing which changes is the door def. wich
corresponds to the icon located in Commands/BBSCmd (stack, type, location,
etc...)

The tooltypes are:

 SYSOP.x= ***             Users who will receive the message
                          eg: Sysop.1=Diogenes
                          Up to 4.294.967.295 "sysops" allowed hehe ;)
                          
                          If you type Sysop.x=EALL   the door will create
                          a public an EALL message instead with a different
                          content. This way, your users can tell you what
                          they think about the refered user.

 PATH= ***                *Very* important ! That's the path to the
                          conference where the mail must be sent.
                          eg: Path=BBS:Amiga
                          with or without terminating "/"
 
 EALL.x=***               That's the conf path where the EALL messages must
                          be sent. You can have several to advertise all
                          traders: PC freaks, Amiga freaks, Console lovers
                          etc...
                          eg: EALL.1=BBS:AmigaWorld
                              EALL.2=BBS:PC
                          Etc...


